168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (This project focuses on the design and implementation of a functional T2 processor using SystemVerilog. The main objective is to develop a processor capable of executing instructions, performing arithmetic and logical operations, transferring data between registers and memory, and controlling the flow of program execution.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The processor consists of several essential components, including the Program Counter \(PC\), Instruction Memory, Data Memory, Registers, Decoder, Multiplexer \(MUX\), and Arithmetic Logic Unit \(ALU\). These components are integrated together to form the processor datapath, allowing instructions to be fetched, decoded, executed, and stored as required. The design also supports memory read and write operations and uses Carry and Zero flags to handle conditional control-flow instructions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
